# Each history: client, w (write) or r (read), value written or returned, start, end (ms).
history H1 one client writes, then reads its write
C1 w 1 0 2
C1 r 1 3 4
end
history H2 a read overlaps a write and sees the old value; a later read sees the new one
C1 w 1 0 10
C2 r 0 2 4
C2 r 1 6 8
end
history H3 stale read: the write finished before the read started, yet the read returns 0
C1 w 1 0 5
C2 r 0 6 8
end
history H4 new then old: C2 sees the new value, later C3 sees the old one
C1 w 1 0 10
C2 r 1 2 4
C3 r 0 6 8
end
history H5 C2 sees the two writes of C1 in the wrong order
C1 w 1 0 2
C1 w 2 3 5
C2 r 2 6 7
C2 r 1 8 9
end
history H6 a client does not see its own write
C1 w 5 0 2
C1 r 0 3 4
end
